1
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:31,557
But I don't want to give up.

2
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:37,617
In the cracks in the bottom of the world.

3
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:40,357
I have been born in the world.

4
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:45,477
I will surely find this way.

5
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:49,097
I will change the world.

6
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:52,240
I will change the world?

7
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:57,860
Thank you.

8
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:27,960
Fighting God!

9
00:01:58,240 --> 00:01:59,257
recent directive now.

10
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:00,177
Here it is.

11
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:03,789
After the initial greeting, it
says he input the information

12
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:07,097
onto this disk when we
boarded the train in Napoli.

13
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:08,497
It goes on, saying,

14
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:10,237
I therefore have no means of knowing the

15
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:12,457
number of your pursuers
at the present moment,

16
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:13,952
nor do I know the number

17
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:17,337
of men you have possibly lost
in your battles until now.

18
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:19,302
This disk will tell you the best

19
00:02:20,060 --> 00:02:22,637
way for us to safely
rendezvous with my daughter.

20
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:24,677
It will be your final mission.

21
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:25,820
Also know this,

22
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:29,837
it is absolutely imperative that you
follow my instructions to the letter.

23
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:30,750
This condition

24
00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:32,697
is non-negotiable.

25
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:37,480
If you or your men deviate from my
directive, regardless of whether the

26
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:43,337
act is accidental, I'll be forced to
consider it an overt act of betrayal.

27
00:02:43,420 --> 00:02:45,220
And now for my directive.

28
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:52,320
You are to travel to the
island of San Giorgiorno Major.

29
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:57,653
There, with my daughter in tow, you
shall go to the top of the bell tower.

30
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:02,654
Upon your safe delivery of my child,
you will have completed the mission.

31
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:04,540
Rule number one.

32
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:06,577
There is no stairway to the top,

33
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:10,131
and only one elevator can reach
the peak of the bell tower.

34
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:14,539
Only Trish and one protector shall
be allowed to board that elevator.

35
00:03:14,700 --> 00:03:15,620
Rule 2.

36
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:18,600
Said protector must have no knives, guns,

37
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:21,367
or cell phones, or any
other objects on them.

38
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:22,840
Rule 3.

39
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:27,728
From the moment you retrieve this disc,
you will have 15 minutes to disembark.

40
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:30,431
This disc is outfitted with a transmitter,

41
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:33,287
which will allow me to
follow your movements.

42
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:35,200
Rule 4.

43
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:38,837
The others must remain on the boat
and are forbidden from coming ashore.

44
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:39,900
That is all.

45
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:42,360
We've made it.

46
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:43,560
Time to do this.

47
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:48,660
So the boss is at the
top of that tower, huh?

48
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:52,579
Well, he's certainly detailed
and extremely careful.

49
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:57,019
But given that he's the head of the
entire organization, makes sense.

50
00:03:57,120 --> 00:04:00,477
It's strange knowing that this
will be the end of our mission.

51
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:01,700
But we're alive.

52
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:03,777
Couldn't ask for more than that.

53
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:06,660
Yeah, we're alive all
right, but just barely.

54
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:08,737
We made it to the City of Water.

55
00:04:08,820 --> 00:04:09,917
We should have some fun.

56
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,357
This place has great cuisine.

57
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:13,322
They've got good chow here, too?

58
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:16,317
I didn't realize how hungry I
was, but my tummy's rumbling.

59
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:18,197
So what are the local specialties?

60
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:21,398
They've got squid ink pasta
and horsehair crab salad,

61
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:24,937
not to mention the carpaccio that's
served at the Hotel Cipriani.

62
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:25,977
It's to die for.

63
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:27,060
Have you lost it?

64
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:30,760
In case you've forgotten,
we are still on assignment!

65
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:34,660
Narancia, keep an eye
on the radar. Uh, sure.

66
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:39,497
Bucciaratti, I would like to offer
myself up to be Trisha's guardian.

67
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:40,697
Let me do this.

68
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:42,956
Let me go with her to the bell tower.

69
00:04:43,780 --> 00:04:46,368
Just who the hell do
you think you are, kid?

70
00:04:46,740 --> 00:04:50,297
Uchirati's our Cape, so he's taking
her to the boss, arrogant prick.

71
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:52,397
The boss would have designated someone to

72
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:55,127
do it himself if he knew
who was still alive.

73
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:59,520
Thank you, but I must go.

74
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:01,480
Let's move, Trish.

75
00:05:01,980 --> 00:05:04,360
Two were requested, and two it shall be.

76
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:14,920
This is it.

77
00:05:15,140 --> 00:05:17,493
Our chance to learn the boss's identity.

78
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:19,060
I won't let it slip by.

79
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:21,120
Listen, Giorno.

80
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:25,833
Given that this is our last mission,
mind lending me a little bit of luck?

81
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:31,337
Some see them as children of the
sun, others as symbols of life.

82
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:33,240
It's like a talisman, yes?

83
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:36,777
Well, I guess so. Yes.

84
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:38,919
Ladybugs are bringers of good luck.

85
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:46,773
This brooch is pulsating with
life thanks to Golden Wind.

86
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,800
It will serve as our beacon.

87
00:05:49,820 --> 00:05:50,650
Bucciarati.

88
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:52,160
Yes, Fugo?

89
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:55,487
This seems the most
fitting time to tell you.

90
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:57,160
Why so formal?

91
00:05:58,420 --> 00:06:02,160
Thing is, I always knew that you
were destined to become Cape.

92
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:05,929
I also know you'll see this
mission through to the very end.

93
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:07,932
Well, of course he will.

94
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:13,920
Together, I know we'll rise
all the way to the top.

95
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:17,060
Yes, that we will.

96
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:19,460
The time's come. Let's go.

97
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:26,696
As long as I can find a way
to affix this to the boss,

98
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:29,668
Giorno will be able to
track his every move.

99
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:33,580
We will unveil the boss's identity.

100
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:35,260
We have to.

101
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:30,280
He left the door open.

102
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:34,606
Our options are the
ground floor or the tower.

103
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:37,540
Straight shot and nowhere to stop.

104
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:38,750
What is...

105
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:41,780
what is going to happen to me?

106
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:45,980
First, I'm kidnapped
by a bunch of mafiosi.

107
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:47,694
My life is threatened.

108
00:07:48,780 --> 00:07:53,133
Then, to top it off, now I'm being
dragged off to a father I've never met.

109
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:57,280
So, where am I supposed to go from here?

110
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:00,700
No need to worry.

111
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:03,200
Your safety is the boss's concern.

112
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:08,160
As for your path moving forward, I
believe I can offer some insight.

113
00:08:09,140 --> 00:08:14,081
You'll be given a different name, after
which you may need to alter your appearance.

114
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:16,893
And you'll likely assume a new identity.

115
00:08:17,420 --> 00:08:19,737
You'll reside somewhere far away from us,

116
00:08:19,820 --> 00:08:22,700
but at long last, you'll
truly know happiness.

117
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:26,700
I assure you, Trish, your
father can make that happen.

118
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:29,780
Here, take my hand.

119
00:08:37,060 --> 00:08:37,890
No.

120
00:08:37,973 --> 00:08:39,740
I'm not afraid.

121
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:41,195
Not in the slightest.

122
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:12,980
I wonder if I'll one day
grow to love my father.

123
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:17,996
Those aren't the kinds of
things families worry about.

124
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:23,810
You're right.

125
00:09:23,893 --> 00:09:25,037
What was I thinking?

126
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:28,420
It's strange to worry my
head over things like that.

127
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:29,770
We're here.

128
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:31,040
This is it.

129
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:40,300
Trish! Trish!

130
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:51,160
What the hell?

131
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:55,777
Her hand? But how?

132
00:09:55,860 --> 00:09:56,817
When did...

133
00:09:56,900 --> 00:10:00,877
We're supposed to be the only
ones currently in this place.

134
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:03,637
The only people who even
know about this are my

135
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:08,460
team and there's no way
could the boss have really

136
00:10:09,140 --> 00:10:14,577
Was this to protect his identity this
mission all the agony we've been through

137
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:20,740
what the hell Was it for did he only lure
us all here to kill her with his own hands

138
00:10:29,640 --> 00:10:34,520
Bruno Bucciarati was born the son of a
fisherman in a small town outside Napoli.

139
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:39,920
Often labeled as standoffish, Bruno's
father lived a life of integrity.

140
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:44,733
More than anything, he fought to protect
his family from life's cruelties.

141
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:48,420
I'm back, Bruno. Papa!

142
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:50,640
The net needs mending.

143
00:10:50,740 --> 00:10:52,040
I've got it.

144
00:10:55,400 --> 00:11:00,180
Bruno's mother had a kind heart, and their
frequent chats always warmed his soul.

145
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:04,040
He especially looked forward
to her nightly bedtime stories.

146
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:06,260
Okay, time for bed.

147
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:12,220
However, everything changed when
Bucciarati was seven. What now?

148
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:13,440
What do you do?

149
00:11:13,820 --> 00:11:16,160
I don't know, but this can't go on.

150
00:11:16,420 --> 00:11:18,700
I need to leave and find my way.

151
00:11:19,820 --> 00:11:22,780
After ten years of marriage,
his parents divorced.

152
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:28,524
No one except his parents would ever know
the reason why their relationship ended.

153
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:30,130
And Bruno?

154
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:31,680
Where'll he stay?

155
00:11:32,760 --> 00:11:35,737
The one thing his parents
agreed on was that the

156
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:38,879
decision of where he would
live was Bruno's to make.

157
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:44,200
Bruno, I want you to know Mama and
Papa love you more than anything.

158
00:11:44,420 --> 00:11:46,596
But we think it's best we live apart.

159
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,600
I'm sorry, my baby.

160
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:50,200
That's how it has to be.

161
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:52,739
But we wanted to give you a choice.

162
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:55,357
Do you want to come with me?

163
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:58,017
Or would you rather stay
and live here with Papa?

164
00:11:58,100 --> 00:12:00,257
You've always been such a bright boy.

165
00:12:00,340 --> 00:12:02,164
You could get a good education.

166
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:05,937
Oh, and there'll be other
kids your age to play with.

167
00:12:06,020 --> 00:12:08,297
You want to come and
live with Mama, right?

168
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:09,520
I know you do.

169
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:15,180
Actually, I think I'll
stay here with Papa. Huh?

170
00:12:16,260 --> 00:12:17,457
You don't mean that.

171
00:12:17,540 --> 00:12:20,000
Bruno, don't make a rash decision.

172
00:12:20,220 --> 00:12:21,985
You've always liked Mama best.

173
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:24,940
I'm staying here and keeping Papa company.

174
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:26,340
You can't!

175
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:31,300
Mama will be alright no
matter where she goes.

176
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:33,380
But Papa...

177
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:39,400
This is goodbye.

178
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:44,260
I promise you, honey,
I'll visit every month.

179
00:12:44,980 --> 00:12:45,810
Yeah.

180
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:55,095
Bucciarati's instincts proved correct.

181
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:59,700
Two years after his mother's departure,
she remarried a Milanese man.

182
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:03,296
After that, he would only
see his mother at Christmas.

183
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:06,999
All that had a curious
effect on her former husband,

184
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:11,396
who became possessed with the idea
of sending his son to a good school.

185
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:15,045
Papa, shouldn't the
customers be arriving soon?

186
00:13:15,220 --> 00:13:16,100
Oh, yeah.

187
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:17,700
I lost track of time.

188
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:20,374
I'll go ahead and recast the nets then.

189
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:21,750
Okay.

190
00:13:21,833 --> 00:13:23,035
This one's all yours.

191
00:13:24,060 --> 00:13:26,317
Bruno's father had always
worked as a fisherman,

192
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:29,157
but now that he was putting
his son through school,

193
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:33,769
he needed to use his boat to make money
with tourists and visiting fishermen.

194
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:37,960
And so, the Wheel of
Destiny steadily turned.

195
00:13:38,500 --> 00:13:39,920
I'm sorry, signore.

196
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:42,057
That island isn't ideal for fishing.

197
00:13:42,140 --> 00:13:42,997
The other one...

198
00:13:43,080 --> 00:13:44,256
I don't give a damn.

199
00:13:44,420 --> 00:13:46,757
We want to go fishing
there, so we're going to go.

200
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:49,637
Just shut up and do your
freaking job, boat man.

201
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:50,550
Got it?

202
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:53,320
Yeah, right away.

203
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:56,160
Later that evening,

204
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:59,037
the Coast Guard would
find Bucciarati's father,

205
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:01,460
his body devastated with bullet wounds.

206
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:04,337
GSWs to the arms, shoulders,
chest, and abdomen.

207
00:14:04,420 --> 00:14:05,250
Seven total.

208
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:06,737
The bullets are still in him.

209
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:07,650
Papa!

210
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:15,440
Please wait until the surgery is over.

211
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:17,057
Just try and calm down.

212
00:14:17,140 --> 00:14:19,552
Are there any family members we can call?

213
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:20,790
Papa.

214
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:26,020
This is evidence.

215
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:27,947
Make sure forensics gets it.

216
00:14:28,680 --> 00:14:30,800
Si, signore. I'm off. Right.

217
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:33,640
How could this have happened?

218
00:14:34,560 --> 00:14:35,420
Good evening.

219
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:36,780
Are you his son?

220
00:14:37,340 --> 00:14:39,281
We found this at the crime scene.

221
00:14:39,860 --> 00:14:43,684
It seems your father became an
accidental witness to a drug deal.

222
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:46,320
He was shot to ensure his silence.

223
00:14:46,740 --> 00:14:49,657
Your father's a very important
witness to this case,

224
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:53,564
so trust me when I say we're all
rooting for him to pull through.

225
00:14:55,100 --> 00:14:55,930
Drugs?

226
00:14:56,013 --> 00:14:57,620
Drugs put my papa in here?

227
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:04,417
Miraculously, Bucciarati's
father survived the surgery.

228
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:08,860
The seven bullets that tore through
his flesh missed critical organs.

229
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:13,297
Those who found him were equipped
with the necessary life-saving tools,

230
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:15,680
buying him time to get to the hospital.

231
00:15:16,020 --> 00:15:17,780
It was a true miracle.

232
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:21,180
But as far as Bucciarati's
life was concerned,

233
00:15:21,520 --> 00:15:25,108
it may have been better if his
father hadn't survived at all.

234
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:30,040
Sometimes, life makes it impossible
to make the right choice.

235
00:15:30,420 --> 00:15:31,560
Life gets messy.

236
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:33,160
Lines get blurred.

237
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:38,980
Damn fisherman.

238
00:15:39,220 --> 00:15:42,500
You just don't know when
to call it quits, do ya?

239
00:15:42,780 --> 00:15:45,260
I'll keep watch, just hurry up and do it!

240
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:48,146
You're a pain for making
us make a night call.

241
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:50,280
Do us all a favor and die!

242
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:55,460
Who the hell are you?

243
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:56,880
You kidding me?

244
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:58,600
It's just some punk kid!

245
00:15:59,260 --> 00:16:00,537
What the hell are you doing?

246
00:16:00,620 --> 00:16:01,561
He's just a kid!

247
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:03,289
Smash the damn knife away!

248
00:16:09,220 --> 00:16:11,573
What the hell do you think you're doing?

249
00:16:22,420 --> 00:16:24,877
I won't let them hurt you, Papa.

250
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:26,078
Leave it all to me.

251
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:28,438
You just worry about getting better.

252
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:30,240
At age 12,

253
00:16:30,620 --> 00:16:32,914
Bruno Bucciarati had become a murderer,

254
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:35,977
and a murderer he would
remain the rest of his life.

255
00:16:36,060 --> 00:16:38,820
I can't turn back now.

256
00:16:39,180 --> 00:16:41,637
Not when they want to
permanently shut us up.

257
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:43,860
And I can't count on the police.

258
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:48,997
The only organization that could
protect them ruled from the shadows.

259
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:50,140
The Family.

260
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:52,960
Ujarati knocked on its doors.

261
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:59,360
And in exchange for his service and
loyalty, protection was finally guaranteed.

262
00:17:00,280 --> 00:17:04,920
He saw it as the embodiment of
justice and gave his all for it.

263
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:09,760
He soon made a name for himself
and caught the eye of Cape Polpo.

264
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:15,440
Five years later, Bucciarati's father
died from complications from his wounds.

265
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:18,917
Bucciarati despised the white
powder of greed that had brought

266
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,647
them into this hell and swore
to battle it with all his might.

267
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:24,790
However...

268
00:17:26,220 --> 00:17:27,200
I'm sorry!

269
00:17:27,460 --> 00:17:28,997
I promise I'll leave him alone!

270
00:17:29,080 --> 00:17:30,537
I'll never bother him again!

271
00:17:30,620 --> 00:17:31,580
That'd be wise.

272
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:34,197
Regret is an emotion
felt only by the living.

273
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:36,560
But if you're a mafioso...

274
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:40,140
What in the hell?

275
00:17:40,740 --> 00:17:41,570
Hey!

276
00:17:41,653 --> 00:17:42,540
What's in the bags?

277
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:46,976
Buterati realized that the
boss, his model of justice,

278
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:49,620
profited from the drugs he so despised.

279
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:52,515
This filth's being peddled in my city?

280
00:17:52,660 --> 00:17:54,660
It was supposed to be prohibited!

281
00:18:00,980 --> 00:18:04,297
Now the boss is our damn boss.

282
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:07,137
His wretchedness makes me want to puke.

283
00:18:07,220 --> 00:18:10,357
Abusing the weak and innocent
is just a means to an end.

284
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:13,969
Profiting from the pain and
suffering of countless citizens?

285
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:15,310
Coward.

286
00:18:15,393 --> 00:18:16,577
You do it to your daughter.

287
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:18,417
You're a fiendish monster.

288
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:22,100
You're a disgrace and you've
You let me down again,

289
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:24,616
but you've done it for the last time!

290
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:33,087
There, Trisha's still alive.

291
00:18:41,420 --> 00:18:42,720
Good, it's stuck.

292
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:45,777
God's hope, I didn't see his face.

293
00:18:45,860 --> 00:18:51,300
At first, I was content with uncovering
your identity, but everything's changed.

294
00:18:51,600 --> 00:18:53,880
After what you've done, die!

295
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:55,310
Think fast.

296
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:58,814
The boss still assumes that
I'm absolutely loyal to him.

297
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:01,700
He'll die by assassination.

298
00:19:05,360 --> 00:19:09,140
I'll ambush him as he tries to
escape and kill the bastard.

299
00:19:22,220 --> 00:19:23,837
Wait, this is...

300
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:24,880
this opening.

301
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:30,500
Of course, the demented bastard
would hide in the crypt of a church.

302
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:34,299
He thinks he can murder
Trish in complete anonymity.

303
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:39,421
His plan must be to pass through the crypt
to escape the building on the other side.

304
00:19:51,320 --> 00:19:53,260
But I'm lying in wait.

305
00:19:57,880 --> 00:19:58,710
There!

306
00:20:18,860 --> 00:20:23,520
In position now leave
while you're still able

307
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:30,880
Bucciarati step out from behind that
pillar and lose your life in the process

308
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:38,800
Go! Zippermen!

309
00:20:45,060 --> 00:20:46,300
He'll rip it off!

310
00:20:57,700 --> 00:20:59,997
Somehow, he figured out I was here.

311
00:21:00,080 --> 00:21:03,720
But now, he's resorted to
hiding in the shadows again.

312
00:21:04,100 --> 00:21:06,688
I need to find his
weakness, whatever it is.

313
00:21:06,820 --> 00:21:09,080
Your rationale intrigues me.

314
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:13,420
Just what were you thinking?

315
00:21:13,780 --> 00:21:16,317
I had a great deal of respect for your

316
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:19,017
excellence and devotion
to the mission until now.

317
00:21:19,100 --> 00:21:22,340
Was your judgment clouded
by your promotion to Cape?

318
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:25,957
Or did your hubris
seduce you into thinking

319
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:28,880
you had the power and
ability to overtake me?

320
00:21:30,100 --> 00:21:35,340
Once Trish regains consciousness, I'll be
sure to let her know you never existed.

321
00:21:35,900 --> 00:21:37,080
Trish, you say?

322
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:39,620
Why bring her into this dispute?

323
00:21:39,940 --> 00:21:43,480
My daughter is of no concern
to you and your ilk demon.

324
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:46,746
You could never understand
what's in my heart.

325
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:51,220
Hey, Giorno.

326
00:21:51,540 --> 00:21:52,952
We're on it, Bucciarati.

327
00:21:53,340 --> 00:21:55,537
Tracking down his movements as we speak.

328
00:21:55,620 --> 00:21:58,797
The brooch will tell me exactly
where he is at all times.

329
00:21:58,880 --> 00:22:01,677
Right now, he's at the bottom
of the stairs to the crypt.

330
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:04,917
He's next to the pillar, about
two meters away from the stairs.

331
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:07,380
But wait, Bucerati! Something's wrong!

332
00:22:07,700 --> 00:22:09,994
Until we know what it is, don't attack!

333
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:15,580
End him!

334
00:22:16,300 --> 00:22:17,130
Zipperman!

335
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:28,148
It wasn't him hiding
in the pillar's shadow.

336
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:29,710
It was me!

337
00:22:34,900 --> 00:22:35,730
What...

338
00:22:35,813 --> 00:22:36,780
what the...

339
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:38,737
What is going on?

340
00:22:38,820 --> 00:22:42,780
Think of this as a gift, a
farewell gift from the heart.

341
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:48,200
In a moment, you will cease to exist,
so I will allow you to know now.

342
00:22:48,360 --> 00:22:52,620
What you witnessed and felt
was your future self laid bare.

343
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:57,057
Simply put, your past
self saw a future version.

344
00:22:57,140 --> 00:23:01,140
Now behold, know the almighty
power of Emperor Crimson.

345
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:04,600
I obliterated time, then leapt beyond it.

346
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:09,580
It doesn't matter who it is.

347
00:23:09,740 --> 00:23:13,740
I shall never allow any Cretan to
threaten my eternal transcendence.

348
00:23:14,020 --> 00:23:14,980
Not ever.

349
00:23:15,540 --> 00:23:18,100
The time's come for you to fade away.

350
00:23:21,660 --> 00:23:25,560
Mucharate, your mission as
protector has been terminated.

351
00:23:26,340 --> 00:23:29,000
Now may the fires of hell embrace you.

352
00:23:56,420 --> 00:23:57,860
Thank you.
